# @lore AU26 C3: same class as the guard artifacts above, one level up — a bare
# `tsc -p packages/db` against a stale `dist/` emits declaration MAPS straight
# into the package source tree (`packages/db/src/*.d.ts.map`); ten of them were
# committed once and only a code review caught them. Emitted maps are never
# sources, in any package.
# `.d.ts` itself is deliberately NOT ignored here — hand-written ambient
# declarations are real sources (`packages/web/src/vite-env.d.ts`,
# `window.d.ts`, `packages/design-system/src/css-modules.d.ts`) — except under
# `packages/db/src`, which has none and is the one tree the emit lands in.
packages/*/src/**/*.d.ts.map
packages/*/src/**/*.js.map
packages/db/src/*.d.ts
# viewer compiled outputs (Vite resolves ./discovery.js → discovery.ts at build/dev time;
# emitted .js/.d.ts/.map files must not be committed)
packages/design-system/viewer/*.js
packages/design-system/viewer/*.d.ts
packages/design-system/viewer/*.js.map
packages/design-system/viewer/*.d.ts.map
# AJ7: same for the annotations/ subdir (the inspector modules)
packages/design-system/viewer/**/*.js
packages/design-system/viewer/**/*.d.ts
packages/design-system/viewer/**/*.js.map
packages/design-system/viewer/**/*.d.ts.map

